{
  "subtype": "faceted_decomposition",
  "concept": "declined_expense_reasons",
  "per_column": [
    {
      "name": "decline_reason",
      "is_constitutive_facet": true,
      "role": "facet",
      "rationale": "Captures the specific reason category for the decline (approval process, not-approved, compliance issue, non-standard). This is a genuine 'aspect of' the decline reason concept -- the substantive ground for declining."
    },
    {
      "name": "compliance_risk",
      "is_constitutive_facet": true,
      "role": "facet",
      "rationale": "Enumerates the compliance-risk dimensions (high value approval, asset tracking, sensitive department, policy violation) that constitute part of why expenses are flagged/declined. It is an aspect of the reasons-and-compliance-risk concept, not an external predictor. Its multi-valued pipe encoding overlaps somewhat with decline_reason (e.g., asset/travel compliance appear in both), weakening exclusivity."
    },
    {
      "name": "is_declined",
      "is_constitutive_facet": false,
      "role": "restatement",
      "rationale": "A binary flag of whether the row is declined. This is the whole condition under which the concept applies, not a facet OF the decline reasons; it restates membership rather than decomposing the reason into aspects."
    }
  ],
  "facet_columns": ["decline_reason", "compliance_risk"],
  "non_facet_columns": ["is_declined"],
  "mutual_exclusivity": 0.5,
  "exhaustiveness": 0.55,
  "rationale": "Two of the three columns (decline_reason, compliance_risk) are genuine meronymic facets of the declined-expense-reasons concept, decomposing it into the substantive ground for decline and the associated compliance-risk aspects. However, is_declined is a restatement of membership in the concept, not a facet of it. Mutual exclusivity is only moderate because decline_reason and compliance_risk share overlapping content (asset approval/tracking, travel compliance, service compliance/agreement appear in both), so they do not cleanly carve non-overlapping aspects. Exhaustiveness is moderate: reason type and compliance risk cover major aspects, but other constitutive facets (e.g., severity, responsible party/policy referenced, remediation status) are absent."
}

